Source provenance
=================

Parts of the Pinduoduo parsing, action rules, browser-login flow, HTTP protocol
handling, protocol diagnostic tools, and the model/tool execution loop and
registry contracts were adapted from:
https://github.com/JC0v0/Customer-Agent

The upstream README declares "MIT". The checked-out source and the upstream
main branch inspected on 2026-10-27 do not contain a standalone LICENSE file;
the GitHub repository metadata reports no detected license. No copyright
holder, year or complete upstream license notice is invented here. Obtain and
preserve the applicable full upstream license/copyright notice before public
redistribution of the derived components.

This is provenance documentation, not a runtime dependency or affiliation.
The new application does not fetch, update from, or link to the upstream
repository during startup or build. Third-party package licenses also apply.

The optional WSL browser-login desktop runs separately installed TigerVNC,
noVNC and websockify. These retain their own licenses (including GPL and MPL);
their binaries and static assets are not vendored into this repository.

